;; A read that returns a value a LATER-COMMITTING confirmed write already
;; replaced -- a genuine stale read (the mirror image of
;; expect-valid-reordered-commit.edn, and the case the old
;; "newest :ok write completed before the read began" rule MISSED).
;;
;; Write 100 completes (t=200). Write 50 is invoked afterwards (t=300, so every
;; linearization orders it after 100) and completes at t=400, before the read
;; begins (t=500). The register therefore holds 50 when the read runs, but the
;; read returns 100 -- the state machine served a value that had already been
;; overwritten.
{:index 0 :time 100 :type :invoke :f :write :value 100 :process 0}
{:index 1 :time 200 :type :ok     :f :write :value 100 :process 0}
{:index 2 :time 300 :type :invoke :f :write :value 50  :process 1}
{:index 3 :time 400 :type :ok     :f :write :value 50  :process 1}
{:index 4 :time 500 :type :invoke :f :read  :value nil :process 2}
{:index 5 :time 600 :type :ok     :f :read  :value 100 :process 2}
